From 71858ca1eeddcf0752ed5d1fa5c33a4459d8beb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiger Kaovilai <passawit.kaovilai@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:40:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(linux): serve the control API in client mode

--control-port / [Control] Listen were server-only. In client mode on
Linux they now serve get_status, get_stats, get_build_info and
get_reorder_stats for this connection, in the server's JSON shape:
get_status lists this connection as the one entry of "clients", and
each path carries the server's per-path keys (srtt/min_rtt/cwnd/bytes/
pkts/loss/state) plus "iface" (bound interface) and "status" (the
library path status). A top-level "state" gives the client state.
add_user/remove_user/list_users and the FEC commands reply
"not supported in client mode".

The library side is one internal snapshot,
mqvpn_client_get_status_snapshot(), since the public
mqvpn_path_info_t has no min_rtt or packet counters.

Signed-off-by: Tiger Kaovilai <passawit.kaovilai@gmail.com>
